#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:8
#: ba2a30e64d094ad88088c535d4f181af
msgid "Command Line Interpreter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:10
#: f702c9ecaecb49dd91db4efc1f4c84f5
msgid "The Mission Planner Command Line interpreter is a serial terminal line editor that works similarly to the way the old DOS prompt operating systems used to work. If you want, you can set up and test APM is via a Command Line Interpreter (CLI). It is only available via the USB cable and it cannot be used via an Xbee or 3DR wireless telemetry connection. Open up the Terminal in the Mission Planner by selecting the Terminal tab (ensure that the serial baud rate is set for 115200). This will bring up the Terminal window, and it should automatically take you to the APM CLI menu (if not, click in the window and hit \"Enter\" three times):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:24
#: a0e2ed6f71064e7b9758197aeee4afac
msgid "You can now enter commands by typing them at the command prompt. You can always type \"exit\" to leave any mode. In the following examples, I'll be using another serial terminal (in this case the Arduino Serial Monitor). You can use any terminal you want, but the Mission Planner terminal is the most straightforward. Here I'm typing \"help\" to see a list of available commands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:35
#: 9fb18b223989481c9a59308770cd7b73
msgid "Initial commands are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:37
#: f8f8a0213fa9411783301d373372db4d
msgid "**logs**: Log readback/setup mode. Used after flying)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:38
#: ac5093dad68441e9883862244e4cb541
msgid "**setup**: Initial setup mode)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:39
#: eacd7bc5b78b4150a6632da1147f0ee1
msgid "**test**: Test mode)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:42
#: 9d8f192620114ea89e6cbb52bdc5d796
msgid "Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:44
#: eb82492d91ec4a7b94ad453594798b92
msgid "The Setup process configures APM for your particular RC radio settings and desired flight modes. Type \"setup\" and hit return to enter this mode. **You MUST setup both radio and modes before you can fly. You should also test that you're getting GPS lock (using the gps command in the test mode), which usually means testing outside where the GPS module has a clear view of the sky.** Allowed setup commands are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:51
#: 7f650591147d4e57946f77fb139c91f2
msgid "**reset**: Resets APM to default settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:52
#: 3640af59639344c180746c74045bbddd
msgid "**radio**: Sets up RC settings (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:53
#: bdc6ec8b747a406b8ce6d209c4c59f4f
msgid "**modes**: Sets up flight control modes for each RC toggle switch position (see below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:54
#: 68b46b6b297a4a3ba1cce296b7b11150
msgid "**compass**: Enables compass. Commands are \"compass on\" or \"compass off\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:56
#: 3b7c1b414df741bfbd8df15547c20beb
msgid "**declination**: Sets local magnetic declination for compass. You can find your local declination at `this web page <http://www.ngdc.noaa.gov/geomag-web/>`__. Although it is given in minutes and seconds, enter it as a decimal. So ``14° 10' E`` would be entered as 14.10."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:60
#: ee7d0463dc3e4f6280b7203386458f18
msgid "**\"battery\"**: Enables battery monitoring. Enter options 0-4 (repeat to enter additional options):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:71
#: f1461c8677e04352b1daf2357b728fde
msgid "**\"show\"**: Shows all current settings in EEPROM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:72
#: fa64b5da1a384125be754bb6a0a6867e
msgid "**\"erase\"**: Erases EEPROM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:75
#: 1d41fa5337ef47f085739cd1fb5d3409
msgid "Radio setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:77
#: 1267de9cd892495b92ad9cef5650b6ac
msgid "*Note: APM does not power the RC receiver or servos (although the RC equipment can power APM). If you have APM powered by USB, you must also connect an ESC/Lipo or receiver battery to the RC APM pins (typically, the ESC would be plugged into Out 3, while a receiver battery would typically be plugged into your receiver, which would send power to APM via the RC cables). If you do not separately power the RC system, APM will be unable to read any signals on its RC inputs.* In this mode you must move both sticks to all of their extremes, as follows: Move the right stick to the top right, then bottom right, then top left, then bottom left. Then repeat for the left stick. The order doesn't matter, but what's important is that you hit all four corners for each stick. Hold the stick in each corner for a second. Here's a screenshot of a typical Radio setup process:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:94
#: cc92c933767443b7be3c3dfa7ca0f54e
msgid "**Note**: As shown above, the RC readings for the channels you have hooked up should be around 1,000-1,300 at the low end and around 1,900-2,000 at the high end. (Readings of exactly 1,000 and 2,000 mean that channel's not connected at all). If you are getting readings that are all around 1,500, there are three likely causes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:100
#: 99636c05c17148579454a1d4c5ea0204
msgid "You didn't move both sticks to all four corners of their range during the test, or did it too quickly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:102
#: d50841d41dcd48589fd253435ecaed17
msgid "Your RC connections are plugged in wrong, either upside down, on the wrong pins, or otherwise not making a connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:106
#: e7c54f5ec264452aa2838f2296d65d45
msgid "Flight Control Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:108
#: fd89441673f04bc09f6fddf6b9714c2a
msgid "Here's how to set your flight control modes: In the CLI, enter setup mode. Type \"modes\" and press return. You can now see the flight modes displayed as you move your control switch to each position. If you want to change your mode, use the rudder/aileron control stick on your radio. Just move the stick to the right or left and the mode will increment. Hitting Enter will exit the mode and save your changes. See this example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:119
#: e906ba7599a34e4e9f9afe9307448824
msgid "**Here's a video tutorial:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:125
#: 2f3e1d53568f47dea5db11cb87ad9878
msgid "Checking for reversed servos"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:127
#: eb54a16940394050ac07bf506f067c68
msgid "Now is a good time to go back and see if any of the DIP switches need to be flip to reverse a servo. Instructions are :ref:`here <plane:reversing-servos-and-setting-normalelevon-mode>`. And remember that if you're flying an elevon plane (flying wing or delta), you should set the mixing with the DIP switch, too. And if you're flying a regular plane and find that channel 1 and 2 are accidentally combined, that means you've accidentally got it in the elevon mode. Push the last DIP switch down to return to normal."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:137
#: 80ba3c7d22ed4e12b82ea877d794ca66
msgid "Logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:139
#: 781125e06d554e548eea30bb2d575676
msgid "This mode allows you to read and manage flight log files in the onboard 16MB dataflash memory. NOTE: You must use erase before trying to use the logging function. Failure to do an erase first will cause problems and show false results."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:144
#: 257c7ddb9a994b0b841f3f3933fa57d4
msgid "**\"dump (n)\"**: Dump log \"n\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:145
#: 6cb0bb15efd34a09b96b1198f5d5c922
msgid "**\"erase\"**: Erase all logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:146
#: ef89fa0c026e4cf4b67bc85931e1fffb
msgid "**\"enable (name) or all\"**: Enable logging \"name\" or everything"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:147
#: 3a25468d19754d4a97b1a20d743b003c
msgid "**\"disable (name) or all\"**: Disable logging \"name\" or everything"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:150
#: 4627fea0e34e4f54b63de3f0cd4827d7
msgid "CLI APM Test Suite"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:152
#: aea8b4e7ab9442dbaa84d116b69e9d75
msgid "APM comes with a number of onboard tests. To use them, type \"test\" in the CLI, and \"help\" to see all the different tests:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:155
#: 3ffb437f835c483f8686d444d86afb80
msgid "**baro**: Shows the data from the barometer"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:156
#: 9d7a06f7c57c4e80b7e3845285396a7b
msgid "**compass**: Shows the data from the magnetometer, if one is connected and enabled"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:158
#: 9b097ce4d98c48f2ae19486edc813142
msgid "**ins**: tests the accelerometers and gyros"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:159
#: c20b735c19394e0cb544154c2f8c00a4
msgid "**optflow**: Tests optical flow sensor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:160
#: 340ebfcbe4ed4fa4902bb0d5aad899f1
msgid "**relay**: Tests the onboard relay (turns it on and off every five seconds; you should hear it faintly click)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/cli-setup-test-modes.rst:162
#: da8796a9024a4298b99d9dd6119d3e20
msgid "**shell**: Provides access to the NSH shell (Pixhawk only)"
msgstr ""

